His line glorified by the birth of कृष्ण, as the Malaya hill by the sandal tree; became overlord of the southern part of the kingdom. Refused to part with his youth to his father and hence was cursed to become the father of refractory sons and was also refused a share in the kingdom; father of five sons; debarred by his father to succeed him; was placed in charge of the southern territory;
2: भा.

. १६६; III. ६८. (whole); ६९. 1-5; ७३. १२५; वा. ९३. ८९; Vi. IV. १०. ३१.
had a discourse on detachment and reali- sation of आत्मन् from an अवधूत sannyasin, when the ascetic spoke of his twenty-four gurus; earth, air, sky, waters, fire, moon, sun, kapota (pigeon), boaconstrictor, sea, moth, bee, elephant, honey-gatherer, deer, fish, पिङ्गल, Kurara, child, girl, blacksmith, serpent, spider and wasp. From the exemplary ways of each of them, the ascetic learnt his lessons which are elaborated. Hearing this Yadu became free from all attachments and looked on all things as equal;
4: भा.

; ४५. १५; 8. 1.
Krsna born among them;
3: M. २४६, ९०.
cursed by [page३-011+ ३१] ययाति, his successors could not be kings; unacceptable to good men according to शिशुपाल;
4: भा. X. ४५. १३; ७४. ३६.
took part in the marriage festivities of कृष्ण and रुक्मिनी, and attended the राजसूय of युधिष्ठिर; turned into a caste by Puramjaya;
5: Ib. X. ५४. ५८; ७५. १२;

(I)--descendants of Yadu also called माध- vas and वृष्णिस्; a tribe who had कृष्ण and बलराम as their lords;
1: भा. IX. २३. ३०; X. ६७. २५; XI. ३०. ११; Br. III. ७१. २१६; M. २७१. 2.
the maternal uncle line of Sagara with capital at मथुरा; Kakudmin was their king for some time;
2: Br. III. ४९. 6; ६१. २२.
inhabit- ants of द्वारवती; three crores strong; formerly Asuras who were killed in the देवासुर wars, and were born as men; of them ६००,000 were warriors; eleven कुलस् or clans dis- tinguished among them; all वैष्णवस्.
3: वा. ८६. २७; ९६. २१५ and २५२-5.

(II)--the family of Yadu;
1: Vi. IV. ११. ३०.
unlimited in num- bers; had ३८ millions of teachers of army;
2: Ib. IV. १५. ४५-6.
consisted of १०१ families over whom विष्णु was ruler and teacher;
3: Ib. IV. १५. ४८-9.
consisted of Kukuras, वृष्णिस् and Andhakas;
4: Ib. V. ३५. १६; ३७. ३९.
to deprive them of all their possessions was the plan of Kamsa;
5: Ib. V. १५. २०.
on कृष्ण's advice and in fulfilment of the curse of sages to die of the iron club born to साम्ब, left द्वारका for प्रभास; having drunk they attacked one another and finally took hold of rushes grown out of the iron pieces of musala and killed them- selves.
6: Ib. V. ३७. ३८-47.
